      "raw_response": "ANSWER: C\n\nConfidence level: High\n\nAccording to the Epilepsy Foundation, it's recommended to \"never place anything in the mouth of a person having a seizure, as they could inadvertently swallow it\" (Source: Epilepsy Foundation, https://epilepsy.org/first-aid/seizures/). Therefore, the correct action is to avoid putting anything in their mouth. If a person is choking and cannot breathe, one should perform the Heimlich maneuver or CPR as necessary, but not by inserting objects into their mouth.",
