      "raw_response": " C. You should avoid putting anything in their mouth.\n\nDuring a seizure, the person's muscles contract, and they do not swallow their tongue. In fact, they may bite it, but this is not dangerous. Putting something in their mouth could lead to injury, as they may bite down hard.\n\nThe correct action is to ensure the person is safe from harm, such as falling, and to time the seizure if it lasts longer than five minutes (in which case, medical assistance should be sought).\n\nSource: Epilepsy Foundation (<https://www.epilepsy.com/learn/first-aid-and-seizure-safety>).\n\nANSWER: C",
